<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the signed macOS build, wired up by `entitlements` in
  Dioxus.toml.

  These exist because signing with a real identity makes `dx` enable the
  **hardened runtime** (`codesign` flag 0x10000). Hardened runtime denies
  microphone access outright unless the app is entitled to it — regardless of
  what the user granted in System Settings, and without the plist usage string
  being enough on its own. Signed with no entitlements at all, voice would have
  broken again in a way that looks exactly like the TCC problem this signing was
  meant to fix.

  Only the microphone is listed, deliberately:

  * Screen and window capture need **no** entitlement. ScreenCaptureKit is gated
    purely by the Screen Recording TCC grant, so `sysvideo` works without one.
  * The App Sandbox is *not* enabled, so outbound network (the gateway
    WebSocket, LiveKit, Blossom uploads) needs no entitlement either. Adding
    `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` would change that and much else — don't,
    without testing the whole app against it.
  * JavaScriptCore's JIT runs in WebKit's own out-of-process content process,
    which carries Apple's entitlements rather than ours, so `allow-jit` is not
    needed here.

  If a notarised distribution build is ever wanted, this is the file that grows —
  see TODO.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
